 schedule before leaving.","short_summary":"A named independent coffee stop anchoring the compact Norse Way business corridor.","evidence_claim":"Wolf's Brew Coffee lists its address as 4145 Norse Way and publishes operating hours on its official website.","source_url":"https://www.wolfsbrewlb.com/","source_title":"Wolf's Brew Coffee","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The official site lists Monday–Friday 8 a.m.–5 p.m. and Saturday–Sunday 8 a.m.–4 p.m.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"csulb-little-coyote-los-coyotes-diagonal","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Little Coyote — Los Coyotes","title":"Order Pizza on Los Coyotes Diagonal","subtitle":"Los Coyotes Diagonal in East Long Beach","notes":"Use the Los Coyotes location—not the separate Retro Row shop—when pizza fits an off-campus lunch or early-evening plan.","short_summary":"A clearly identified pizza destination directly on the diagonal corridor northeast of campus.","evidence_claim":"Little Coyote's official site identifies its Los Coyotes location at 3500 N. Los Coyotes Diagonal and publishes weekday hours.","source_url":"https://littlecoyotelbc.com/","source_title":"Little Coyote: Long Beach Pizza Shop & More","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The official site lists the Los Coyotes location Monday–Friday, noon–9 p.m.; verify before a weekend trip.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"csulb-el-dorado-nature-center-spring-street","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"El Dorado Nature Center","title":"Follow the Trails off Spring Street","subtitle":"Spring Street at the San Gabriel River","notes":"Enter from Spring Street, cross the wooden bridge, and choose the paved quarter-mile route or the longer dirt trails.","short_summary":"A trail-and-lake destination that turns the Spring Street corridor into a nature excursion.","evidence_claim":"The City describes a 105-acre habitat at El Dorado Nature Center with two miles of dirt trails, a quarter-mile paved trail, lakes, a stream, and a visitor center.","source_url":"https://longbeach.gov/park/park-and-facilities/parks-centers-pier/el-dorado-nature-center/","source_title":"El Dorado Nature Center","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The official page lists daily vehicle-parking charges; consult posted trail and service-dog rules before visiting.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"csulb-2nd-and-pch-pacific-coast-highway","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"2ND & PCH","title":"Photograph the Marina-Facing Center","subtitle":"Pacific Coast Highway at Second Street","notes":"Use the center's visitor guidance to photograph its public-facing spaces, while respecting restricted and private areas.","short_summary":"A map-listed shopping center where the official visitor page expressly addresses guest photography.","evidence_claim":"2ND & PCH lists its address as 6480 East Pacific Coast Highway and states that photography is encouraged subject to its guidelines.","source_url":"https://2ndandpch.com/visit/","source_title":"Visit — 2ND & PCH","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Center hours are listed as Monday–Saturday 10 a.m.–9 p.m. and Sunday 11 a.m.–7 p.m.; photography guidelines apply.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"csulb-recreation-park-seventh-street","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Recreation Park","title":"Choose a Sport on Seventh Street","subtitle":"East Seventh Street west of campus","notes":"Arrive from Seventh Street and choose among the picnic area, playground, courts, casting pond, community center, or fields.","short_summary":"A large civic recreation complex that supports several different kinds of daytime outings.","evidence_claim":"The City locates Recreation Park at 4900 E. 7th St. and lists amenities including a casting pond, playground, picnic area, tennis center, fields, and community center.","source_url":"https://www.longbeach.gov/Park/Park-and-Facilities/Directory/Recreation-Park/","source_title":"Recreation Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Some facilities, classes, golf, and reserved picnic uses have separate contacts or fees; check the city page before planning them.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"csulb-los-altos-library-britton-drive","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Los Altos Neighborhood Library","title":"Use the Library on Britton Drive","subtitle":"Britton Drive in Los Altos","notes":"Bring a device for the free Wi-Fi or use a public computer, and check the branch calendar if you want to pair the stop with an event.","short_summary":"A neighborhood-library stop with connectivity, computers, accessible facilities, and bike parking.","evidence_claim":"The City locates Los Altos Neighborhood Library at 5614 E. Britton Dr. and lists public computers, free Wi-Fi, accessible facilities, and a bike rack.","source_url":"https://longbeach.gov/library/locations/losaltos/","source_title":"Los Altos Neighborhood Library","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The branch is closed Sunday and Monday; the official page lists Tuesday–Saturday hours that vary by day.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"csulb-art-theatre-fourth-street","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Art Theatre Long Beach","title":"Catch an Independent Film on Fourth Street","subtitle":"East Fourth Street on Retro Row","notes":"Check the current calendar before heading to the Fourth Street marquee, since films, discussions, and special programs rotate.","short_summary":"A historic independent cinema that gives the Fourth Street corridor a specific cultural destination.","evidence_claim":"The Art Theatre identifies its location at 2025 E. 4th St. and describes itself as an independent Long Beach cinema operating since the 1920s.","source_url":"https://arttheatrelongbeach.org/","source_title":"Art Theatre Long Beach","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Screenings and program times vary; consult the official calendar and ticket details before traveling.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
